From e2a43295b7f6684c8fe92226058ba793aa227b22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 05:18:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Facebook page hygiene rule across generator, validator and
 review

A Facebook value is not usable data when the URL contains a /p/, /php/ or
/people/ path segment, or when the page is shown as a "Fan Page"/fanpage.
Apply this consistently on all three surfaces:

- generator (metadata_fetcher.verify_socials): drop such facebook_page values
  during discovery, before the live-URL gate, so they never reach the export
  or the review's expected value
- validator (validator.py): new facebook_page_hygiene check + DEFAULT_RULES
  entry -> the cell fails
- review (app.py _review_compare): /php/ added to the bad-URL patterns and a
  guard so a bad manual value is always flagged, even with no discovered value

Adds test_facebook_rules.py (17 tests) covering all three surfaces.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
